assistant: Subject: follow next_cursor when searching products

The 2026-10-01 vendor API pages `/products` results. It returned 5 items with `total: 7` and `next_cursor: "5"`, but `search_products` only read the first page and dropped the cursor, so the list came back incomplete. The handler in `src/tools/search_products.ts` now keeps requesting `&cursor=<next_cursor>` and adding each page's items until `next_cursor` is null. On v1 `next_cursor` is always null, so only one request is made and the fixtures produce the same output as before. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass. One thing I did not fix: in the recorded v2 response every price is exactly 100× its v1 value (6900 vs 69), which suggests the new version sends prices in cents. Neither the spec nor the response says what unit prices are in, so I didn't add a ÷100 conversion. That needs confirming with the vendor before it is changed in its own fix.

